        <item>
            <title>1.10.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 20:03:20 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.10.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.10.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>New</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Drive Vox from Shortcuts and Siri.</strong> The “Speak Selection” and “Speak Text” actions now work reliably — no more “Shortcuts couldn’t communicate with the app.” Vox runs the action in the background, so the app you’re working in keeps focus.</li>
                    <li><strong>New “Listen and Transcribe” action.</strong> Start dictation from a Shortcut: Vox records, transcribes on-device, and hands the text back to the Shortcut so you can pipe it anywhere — notes, messages, automations. It stops automatically when you stop talking.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Fixed</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>A broken speech-model download no longer sticks dictation at “Model not ready.”</strong> Vox now detects an incomplete model on disk, cleans it up, and re-downloads it automatically — and a Download button appears on the model card so you’re never stuck.</li>
                    <li><strong>Switching the Listening latency tier is smoother.</strong> The new tier loads immediately after switching, and previously downloaded tiers stay cached so switching back is instant.</li>
                    <li>Clearer error messages when a Shortcut can’t run (model still downloading, microphone permission needed).</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
